     "citations": null,
     "text": "{\"completeness\": 0.9, \"citation_quality\": 0.85, \"severity_defensibility\": 0.9, \"overall_pass\": true, \"feedback\": \"This is a strong triage submission. The analyst correctly identified three relevant ATT&CK techniques with solid justification for the PowerShell command execution, obfuscation, and ingress tool transfer. The severity assessment is well-reasoned and appropriately graduated\u2014high rather than critical, with clear acknowledgment of what would escalate it further (confirmed execution or active C2). The recommended response is thorough and operationally sound. Minor areas for enhancement: T1027 (Obfuscation) could be better justified with specific examples of what obfuscation techniques are present in the command line (the -NoProfile and -WindowStyle Hidden are more about execution evasion than content obfuscation); and including a brief note on potential false positive vectors (e.g., legitimate administrative PowerShell scripts) would strengthen defensibility, though this appears unlikely given the indicators.\"}",
